---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SECTIONS } from "../data/sections";

const title = "Best Treadmill Covers (2026): Garage, Indoor and Outdoor Picks";
const description =
  "Four treadmill covers checked against their listings, for folding, non-folding and garage use, plus how to measure your machine and avoid trapping condensation.";

const PRODUCTS = [
  {
    id: "clawscover-folding",
    name: "ClawsCover Folding Treadmill Cover",
    brand: "ClawsCover",
    category: "Cover for folding treadmills stored upright",
    badge: "Best for Folding Treadmills",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08LW37LFK?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31WDCfK+XCL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$28–$48",
    priceBounds: {"low":28,"high":48},
    specs: "46 x 38 x 66 in. (D x W x H) · 420D polyester Oxford",
    pros: [
      "The 46 x 38 x 66-inch shape suits the common upright folded position",
      "420D polyester Oxford fabric, confirmed in the listing title, bullets and table",
      "Adjustable elastic drawstring at the base for windy spots",
      "Comes with a storage bag, so the cover is easy to put away between sessions",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Coated fabric rather than breathable cloth, so leave the hem loose in a humid garage",
      "Too small for non-folding machines; this is a folded-position cover only",
      "The same listing number has appeared under a different cover title in another language version, so confirm the style you have selected",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The default cover for a folding treadmill kept upright indoors or in a closed garage. Measure the machine folded first.",
    description: "ClawsCover sells this cover for folding treadmills in the upright stored position, and its Amazon listing gives the same 46 x 38 x 66-inch size in its title, its bullet points and its specification table, which is less common than it should be. A second retailer listing for the ClawsCover folding cover gives the same size, and an independent roundup describes the brand's covers as 420D polyester Oxford with a coated interior, which matches the listing. The listing describes double-stitched seams, a hook-and-loop closure and an adjustable elastic drawstring at the base, and the package includes a storage bag. It is sold alongside an unfolding version for non-folding machines, so check which style is selected before you order. Two cautions. This is a coated fabric, so in a garage leave the hem loose and never put it over a damp or warm machine. And we saw the same listing number attached to an under-desk cover in another language version of the page, so confirm the size on the listing you are buying from.",
  },
  {
    id: "clawscover-unfolding",
    name: "ClawsCover Unfolding Treadmill Cover",
    brand: "ClawsCover",
    category: "Long, low cover for non-folding treadmills",
    badge: "Best for Non-Folding Treadmills",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08F779H3M?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31WDCfK+XCL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$29",
    priceBounds: {"low":29,"high":29},
    specs: "79 x 38 x 60 in. (L x W x H) · 420D polyester Oxford · elastic hem",
    pros: [
      "The 79 x 38 x 60-inch shape covers most full-size non-folding machines to near the floor",
      "Elastic hem holds it on without a drawstring to fiddle with",
      "Reflective strips and a handle, useful in a dim garage",
      "Same fabric as the folding version, at almost the same price",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Machines longer than about 79 inches or taller than about 60 need a made-to-measure cover",
      "Coated fabric, not breathable cloth; avoid sealing it tight in a humid space",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The straightforward choice for a non-folding treadmill indoors or in a garage, if your machine fits inside 79 x 38 x 60 inches.",
    description: "This is the non-folding sibling of the ClawsCover folding cover, sold on the same Amazon listing under an Unfolding style option. Its listing gives 79 inches long, 60 high and 38 wide, made of 420D polyester Oxford, and an independent roundup of treadmill covers names the same ClawsCover unfolding model with the same size and fabric. That is the long, low shape of a full-size treadmill that does not fold. The listing describes double-stitched seams, reflective strips with a handle, an elastic hem at the base and waterproofing strips inside the seams, and roundup coverage describes the same elastic hem and reflective details. The size is the thing to check: measure your machine's overall length including the motor hood and rear roller housing, and the height to the top of the console, and compare. Many commercial-style machines are longer than 79 inches. Like most coated covers, it sheds drips rather than breathing freely, so in a humid garage leave the hem loose and keep the machine dry before covering it.",
  },
  {
    id: "zettum-600d-unfolding",
    name: "Zettum 600D Treadmill Cover (Unfolding)",
    brand: "Zettum",
    category: "Heavier PU-coated cover for carports and patios",
    badge: "Best Weatherproof",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DXKGJ8MF?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41Ti0Z-0HVL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$40",
    priceBounds: {"low":40,"high":40},
    specs: "79 x 38 x 60 in. · 600D Oxford with PU coating · drawstring hem",
    pros: [
      "Heavier 600D fabric than the 420D covers, for a carport, patio or draughty garage",
      "PU-coated to shed water, with a drawstring to stop wind lifting it",
      "Quick-drying surface the maker says can be rinsed and wiped clean",
      "Same long, low shape as other non-folding covers",
    ],
    cons: [
      "The folding version of this cover gives two conflicting sizes in its listing, so we have not listed it",
      "No vents or zip described; the heavier coating breathes less, so watch for moisture inside",
      "The three-year UV resistance figure is the maker’s own test claim",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For a non-folding treadmill under a carport or patio roof, or in a garage that is open to the weather. Not a substitute for keeping the machine indoors.",
    description: "Zettum's unfolding treadmill cover is listed at 79 x 38 x 60 inches in 600D Oxford fabric with a polyurethane coating, and an independent roundup of treadmill covers names it with the same size and fabric. Its own table labels the 79-inch figure as width, but the three numbers agree everywhere. The heavier fabric is the reason to choose it over the 420D covers: it is the one we would put over a machine in an open carport, under a patio roof or in a garage with a door that is often open. The listing describes a windproof drawstring and a quick-drying surface that can be rinsed and wiped, and the maker claims at least three years of UV resistance from its own testing; roundup coverage repeats that claim, but it is the maker's figure, not an independent one. Neither source describes vents or a zip. Because heavier coated fabric breathes less, leave it loose when the weather is calm and take it off if you see moisture inside. Zettum also sells a folding version, but its listing gives two different sizes, so we have left it out.",
  },
  {
    id: "rilime-waterproof-treadmill-cover-81x37x67",
    name: "Rilime Waterproof Treadmill Cover (81 x 37 x 67 in.)",
    brand: "Rilime",
    category: "Oversized cover for machines that outgrow the standard size",
    badge: "Best for Larger Machines",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B089RDDB5Y?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41YGRJ95pPL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $31 (Amazon, 9 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":31,"high":31},
    specs: "Larger than the standard 79 x 38 x 60 in. non-folding size, per the listing · zip opening · drawstring hem · silver-coated oxford fabric",
    pros: [
      "Listed at 81 x 37 x 67 inches: longer and taller than the standard non-folding size, for machines with a high console",
      "A zip along one side, so it can go on and off a large machine without lifting it over the console",
      "A drawstring hem to hold it in place in a draughty garage",
      "A fraction of the price of a made-to-measure cover",
    ],
    cons: [
      "We found no second source for its size or fabric, so measure against the listing before ordering",
      "No vents described; like any coated cover, it can trap moisture in a damp garage",
      "An inch narrower than the 38-inch standard covers, so check the width of wide machines",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For a long or tall treadmill that a standard 79 x 38 x 60-inch cover will not clear, if its listed size fits your measurements.",
    description: "The cover we would have recommended for odd-sized machines, Covers & All’s made-to-measure treadmill cover with air vents, is sold on the maker’s own site rather than on Amazon. The nearest thing on Amazon is a larger standard size, and this Rilime cover is the one we found that is listed bigger than the usual 79 x 38 x 60 inches in both length and height. Its Amazon title and bullet points agree on 81 x 37 x 67 inches (206 x 94 x 170 cm), describe 210D oxford fabric with a silver-plated undercoating and interior bound seams, a zip for access and a drawstring hem, and say it suits most folding and non-folding treadmills. We could not find a second retailer listing or an independent review that confirms those figures for this exact product, so treat them as the seller’s, and measure your machine, console included, before ordering; note that it is an inch narrower than the 38-inch standard covers. It describes no vents, so in a damp garage follow the condensation advice below and leave the hem loose. Amazon showed it at $30.99 on 9 November 2026. If you need a true made-to-measure cover with vents, buy direct from a maker such as Covers & All.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Buying Guides", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/guides/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Best Treadmill Covers", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best-treadmill-covers/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Should I put a cover on my treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "If the treadmill sits in a garage, a dusty room, near a window, or goes unused for weeks, a cover is worth having: it keeps dust off the belt, sun off the console and some damp off the frame. If you use the machine daily in a clean indoor room, wiping it after each session and vacuuming around it matters more than a cover.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What size treadmill cover do I need?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Measure the machine in the position you will cover it. Fold a folding treadmill and measure height, widest width and depth; measure a non-folding machine as it stands, including the motor hood and rear roller housing. Choose a cover a few inches larger in each direction. Folding machines commonly suit about 46 x 38 x 66 inches; non-folding about 79 x 38 x 60.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is a waterproof treadmill cover good for a garage?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It can be, used carefully. A coated cover sheds drips and slows temperature swings, but it breathes less than plain fabric, so moisture already under it can condense when the garage cools. Only cover a dry machine, leave the hem loose unless it is windy, prefer a cover with vents, and run a dehumidifier if the garage is damp.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can I leave a treadmill outside under a cover?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Not as a long-term plan. Most treadmill manuals specify indoor use, and environmental damage may not be covered by the warranty. A heavy, coated cover reduces exposure under a carport or patio roof, but it does not make the motor, controller or console weatherproof. If the machine has to live outdoors, choose one built for it.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can I cover my treadmill right after using it?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "No. The motor and controller are still warm after a session, and a cover traps that heat and any sweat on the frame. Switch the treadmill off, unplug it, take the safety key out, wipe off sweat, and let the machine cool and dry before covering it. Never cover a treadmill that is running.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is a plastic sheet or tarp OK as a treadmill cover?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It is the worst choice in a garage or basement. Plastic sheeting and tarpaulins trap humid air against the machine, and when the temperature drops, water condenses on the inside and drips onto the frame and console. A fabric treadmill cover, or a cotton or canvas dust sheet, is better. If plastic is all you have, leave the bottom open.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-10-15",
      dateModified: "2026-10-15",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      ...(product.brand ? { brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.brand } } : {}),
      ...(product.image ? { image: product.image.url } : {}),
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              url: product.amazonUrl,
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 4,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best-treadmill-covers/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/best-treadmill-covers/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "guides");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const MORE = (GROUP?.pages ?? []).filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-10-15",
    modifiedTime: "2026-10-15",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "treadmill cover",
      "best treadmill cover",
      "treadmill cover for garage",
      "outdoor treadmill cover",
      "folding treadmill cover",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Best for Folding Treadmills: ClawsCover Folding Treadmill Cover", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/guides/">Buying Guides</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Buying Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Best Treadmill Covers for Garage and Home</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        A treadmill cover is a simple product with two ways to go wrong: the wrong size, and the wrong fabric for the room. Here are four covers whose listed size and material we could confirm, and the measuring, condensation and safety rules that decide which one you need.
      </p>
      <p class="ed-answer"><strong>Short answer.</strong> Best for Folding Treadmills: <a href="#clawscover-folding">ClawsCover Folding Treadmill Cover</a>. Best for Non-Folding Treadmills: <a href="#clawscover-unfolding">ClawsCover Unfolding Treadmill Cover</a>. Best Weatherproof: <a href="#zettum-600d-unfolding">Zettum 600D Treadmill Cover (Unfolding)</a>.</p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated October 15, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We research every product on this page independently. If you buy through our links, we may earn a
        commission at no cost to you. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Learn more about how we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#clawscover-folding"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31WDCfK+XCL._SL500_.jpg" alt="ClawsCover Folding Treadmill Cover" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#clawscover-unfolding"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31WDCfK+XCL._SL500_.jpg" alt="ClawsCover Unfolding Treadmill Cover" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#zettum-600d-unfolding"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41Ti0Z-0HVL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Zettum 600D Treadmill Cover (Unfolding)" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>ClawsCover Folding Treadmill Cover · ClawsCover Unfolding Treadmill Cover · Zettum 600D Treadmill Cover (Unfolding)</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          Most treadmill covers are sold by marketplace brands under near-identical titles, and the
          listings are often careless: the same cover described at two different heights, a
          specification table that contradicts its own bullet points, a fabric named one way in
          the title and another in the description. That makes the size and material — the two
          things that actually matter — harder to trust than they should be. The four covers below
          are the ones whose figures held up across more than one source, and the guide after them
          covers measuring your machine, choosing between a dust cover and a weatherproof one, and
          the condensation problem that a cover can make better or worse.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best for Folding Treadmills:</span> <a href="#clawscover-folding">ClawsCover Folding Treadmill Cover</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best for Non-Folding Treadmills:</span> <a href="#clawscover-unfolding">ClawsCover Unfolding Treadmill Cover</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Weatherproof:</span> <a href="#zettum-600d-unfolding">Zettum 600D Treadmill Cover (Unfolding)</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best for Larger Machines:</span> <a href="#rilime-waterproof-treadmill-cover-81x37x67">Rilime Waterproof Treadmill Cover (81 x 37 x 67 in.)</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[3].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <aside class="ed-note not-prose">
          <span class="ed-note-k">What we checked</span>
          <strong class="text-gray-900">On the products below.</strong> We have not tested these
          covers. The Rilime cover was checked on 9 November 2026 against its Amazon listing only, as its
          card explains. The others were checked on 15 October 2026 against its Amazon listing or the maker's own
          site, and against at least one second source — another retailer listing or an independent
          roundup — for size, fabric and current availability. A figure appears on this page only
          where those sources agreed; where a listing contradicted itself or another source, we left
          the figure out and say so. Prices are the ones we saw on that date and change often, so
          confirm the size and the style you have selected on the exact listing before ordering. We
          earn a commission if you buy through the Amazon links on this page; it does not change
          which products we list or what we say about them.
        </aside>

        <nav class="ed-toc not-prose" aria-label="In this guide">
          <h2>In this guide</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#quick-picks">Our Picks at a Glance</a></li>
            <li><a href="#picks">The 4 Best Treadmill Covers</a></li>
            <li><a href="#how-we-chose">How We Chose These Covers</a></li>
            <li><a href="#measuring">How to Measure Your Treadmill for a Cover</a></li>
            <li><a href="#indoor-vs-weatherproof">Indoor Dust Covers Versus Weatherproof Covers</a></li>
            <li><a href="#condensation">Condensation, and Why Breathability Matters in a Garage</a></li>
            <li><a href="#safety">Covering Safely: Heat, Power, Pets and Children</a></li>
            <li><a href="#fitting-and-care">Putting a Cover On, and Looking After It</a></li>
            <li><a href="#walking-pads">Walking Pads and Under-Desk Treadmills</a></li>
            <li><a href="#who-should-skip">Who Does Not Need a Treadmill Cover</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <div id="quick-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Our Picks at a Glance</h2>
<p>
            The first decision is not the brand but the shape of your machine. A folding treadmill
            stored upright needs a tall, short cover; a <a href="/best-non-folding-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>non-folding treadmill</a> needs a long, low one;
            and a treadmill in a damp garage or under a carport needs a heavier fabric and, ideally,
            vents. Pick the row that matches your machine and your room.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[480px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr>
              <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Pick</th>
              <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Best for</th>
              <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Why</th>
            </tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">ClawsCover Folding Treadmill Cover</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Folding treadmills, indoors or in a garage</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">46 x 38 x 66 in., 420D polyester Oxford, the usual folded-machine shape</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">ClawsCover Unfolding Treadmill Cover</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Non-folding treadmills</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">79 x 38 x 60 in., the same fabric, with an elastic hem</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Zettum 600D Treadmill Cover (Unfolding)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Carports, patios and harsher garages</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Heavier 600D PU-coated fabric in the same 79 x 38 x 60 in. size</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Rilime Waterproof Treadmill Cover (81 x 37 x 67 in.)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Long or tall machines</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Listed larger than the standard 79 x 38 x 60 in., with a zip side</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            If the treadmill is going into a garage, read our guide to <a href="/treadmill-in-garage/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">keeping a treadmill in a garage</a> first. A cover is one of several defences against cold, damp and dust out there, and it
            is not the most important one.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>The 4 Best Treadmill Covers</h2>
<p>
            Each card gives the sizes and materials we could confirm in two places (the Rilime card,
            which stands in for a made-to-measure cover not sold on Amazon, says where we could not),
            the price we saw, and who the cover suits. The size line matters more than anything else on the
            card: a cover that is too small will not go on, and one that is far too big pools on the
            floor, catches feet and lets wind underneath.
